<title>SWEDEN: Skanska/Taylor Woodrow to build embassy in Moscow.</title>
<headline>Skanska/Taylor Woodrow to build embassy in Moscow.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish construction firm Skanska on Thursday said its Finnish division was to build a new British embassy in Moscow worth several hundred million crowns in conjunction with Britain's Taylor Woodrow.</p>
<p>The order to the Skanska Oy, will be split 50:50 with Taylor Woodrow. It was awarded by the British Foreign Office.</p>
<p>The new embassy will be built on the eastern side of the Moscow river, two kms west of the Kremlin, and will include offices, flats, and parking for embassy staff.</p>
<p>The work is expected to be finished in May 1999.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
